the algorithms that the FHRPY package re-implements.

WHY THEY ARE HERE
-----------------
They are included ONLY as a numerical PARITY REFERENCE: the Octave harness in
this directory runs the original FHRMA code so that the independent NumPy ports
in fhrpy/ can be validated for numerical faithfulness. They are NOT imported,
linked, or shipped as part of the FHRPY Python package (which is MIT-licensed).
They are build/test tooling, executed inside an isolated Docker container.

This separation (GPLv3 reference code used only to test an independent MIT
implementation, never distributed within the package) keeps the FHRPY package
itself MIT-licensed. If these reference files are ever distributed, they remain
under GPLv3 and must be accompanied by this notice and the full GPLv3 text
(see the LICENSE file in the upstream FHRMA repository).

